-- title:
--   Image of a k(X)-valued map integral over k[b₀]
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $B$ a commutative ring equipped with a $k$-algebra structure, and let $b_0 \in B$. Assume that every element $b$ of $B$ is integral over the $k$-subalgebra $\mathrm{Algebra.adjoin}\,k\,\{b_0\} \subseteq B$ generated by $b_0$, i.e. satisfies a monic polynomial equation with coefficients in that subalgebra. Let $\psi \colon B \to \mathrm{RatFunc}\,k$ be a homomorphism of $k$-algebras into the field of rational functions over $k$, and suppose $\psi(b_0) = X$. The conclusion is an equality of $k$-subalgebras of $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,k$: the range of $\psi$ coincides with the range of the evaluation homomorphism $\mathrm{Polynomial.aeval}\,X \colon k[T] \to \mathrm{RatFunc}\,k$ sending $T$ to $X$, that is, with the image of the polynomial ring $k[X]$ inside $k(X)$. Thus under these hypotheses $\psi(B)$ is exactly the copy of $k[X]$ in $k(X)$, neither larger nor smaller.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a ring integral over $k[b_0]$, mapped to the rational function field so that $b_0 \mapsto X$, has image precisely $k[X]$, because $k[X]$ is integrally closed in $k(X)$. It is used in the identification of a residue ring arising from a valuation subring with a polynomial ring, via [`ValuationSubring.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_polynomial_zmod_of_residue_generated`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_polynomial_zmod_of_residue_generated).
